    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> adamrk submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#pullrequestreview-5032062260\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 619311401,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787757134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#discussion_r3864108250\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Since we're now consuming the fuel after the fuel check, a bunch of these tests need an additional fuel check inserted at the end to pass. The empty loop block does that.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 619311404,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787757135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#discussion_r3864177432\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm not sure what to do with these saturating fuel tests. Now that we only consume the fuel on a successful operation we shouldn't be able to actually hit the saturation.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 619311405,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787757135
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#pullrequestreview-5033631474\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 619351227,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787767583
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#discussion_r3865449477\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could the fuel check move to after the operation instead of before the operation to handle this? That way while the fuel running out would be retroactively discovered it'd basically be the same thing and wouldn't need extra updates</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 619351229,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787767584
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> adamrk submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#pullrequestreview-5033901495\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 619358288,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787769438
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> adamrk created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#discussion_r3865681035\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah we can do that. I think it'll require changing some other tests which assert that we don't do a bulk operation if fuel is at 0 just before the op, but that seems fine to me.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 619358289,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787769438
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#pullrequestreview-5035568167\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 619396233,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787783079
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#discussion_r3867193612\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah that seems ok to me, a lot of the fuel tests are about precise behavior and it's ok to tweak them if the behavior is slightly adjusted as well</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 619396234,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1787783079
