    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#issuecomment-5496416968\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213\">PR #14213</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Looks like the merge queue failure was a real failure from an oob test case now trapping with a different error and the test should be changed. I'm not sure why that wasn't picked up on the PR CI run?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620705104,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788276911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#issuecomment-5496519124\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213\">PR #14213</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh we've got some <a href=\"https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-ci.html\">more information here</a> but CI on PRs is a subset of the CI run in the merge queue (it'd be a bit too expensive to run everything on every PR)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620707514,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788277391
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#issuecomment-5496537806\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213\">PR #14213</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I see it was a failure on i686. Makes sense that we don't run that on every PR.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620707943,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788277477
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213\">PR #14213</a>.</p>",
        "id": 620751218,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788286182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213#issuecomment-5498351768\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14213\">PR #14213</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So the i686 failure was actually an unrelated bug that was just uncovered by this change:<br>\nWhen handling <code>table.grow</code> we would trap with an OOB error if the delta couldn't fit in a native <code>usize</code>, meaning on 32-bit host a 64-bit table grow by more than <code>u32::MAX</code> would trap when it should actually return -1.</p>\n<p>It's just a one line fix so I included it here along with an explicit test for this behavior. </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 620752628,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1788286487
    },
